\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item DerSimonian-Laird with a normal reference: the interval and p-value do not widen for few studies (no Hartung-Knapp adjustment), so treat a pooled estimate from two or three studies with care.
\item A feature with one study is reported with tau2 = 0 and q, i_squared and leave_one_out_max_delta null.
\item Each feature is pooled on its own and p_value is not adjusted across features; send the p_value column to stats adjust.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. 
